As someone who is converting rpg maker MZ to monogame for the fun,
you will be surprised with HOW much leverage C# gives you.
Ok sure doing plugin is SLIGHTLY more complex but its just a matters of Factories and Hooks
this what I basically do for the GameSystem class so u can easily hooks new field to save without needing a factory or Reflections.
Code:
public virtual T GetCustomField<T>(string field) where T : class
{
    return _customField[field] as T;
}
public virtual void OnBeforeSave()
{
    _saveCount++;
    _versionId = DataManager.DataSystem.VersionId;
    _framesOnSave = Engine.FrameCount;
    _bgmOnSave = AudioManager.SaveBgm();
    _bgsOnSave = AudioManager.SaveBgs();
    OnBeforeSaveHook?.Invoke();
}

public virtual void OnAfterLoad()
{
    Engine.FrameCount = _framesOnSave;
    AudioManager.PlayBgm(_bgmOnSave);
    AudioManager.PlayBgs(_bgsOnSave);

    OnAfterLoadHook?.Invoke();
}
that pretty easily TBH.
